-- Explicitly deny insert/update/delete on org_members for all authenticated users via RLS policies (no policies = no access by default for insert/update/delete if we don't create them)
-- Since no INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE policies are created for org_members, only service_role can do it directly. 
-- However, to be explicit about R4 "Apart from accept_invite, nobody can add or change memberships":
-- We rely on the absence of policies for INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on org_members for authenticated users.
-- But we must ensure the RPC function can still work. The RPC function will run as the user by default unless specified SECURITY DEFINER.
-- To allow the RPC to insert, we will make the RPC function SECURITY DEFINER and grant execute.
